## Workflow

### Branching Strategy
- `main`: stable, deployable.
- `dev`: integration branch (optional).
- Feature branches: `feat/<short-name>`, fixes: `fix/<short-name>`.

### Development
- Install deps in `frontend`: `npm install`.
- Run dev server: `npm run dev`.
- Keep ESLint clean; fix warnings when reasonable.

### Pull Requests
- Open PRs from feature branches to `dev` (or `main` if no `dev`).
- Checklist: description, screenshots, and docs alignment.
  - Reference and, if needed, update `PRD.md` for any product/requirement changes.
  - Reference and, if needed, update `UI_UX.md` for any UI/UX or component pattern changes.
  - Note any deviations from `generate.mdc` or `workflow.mdc` and justify.cd
- Request review; address comments promptly.

### Environments & Config
- Frontend env: Vite `import.meta.env` for API base URL.
- Backend env: `MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`, SMTP creds, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, `CLIENT_URL`.
- Do not commit `.env` files.

### Documentation Source of Truth
- Product scope and requirements: `PRD.md` (full‑stack).
- UI and interaction guidelines: `UI_UX.md`.
- Code generation and contribution rules: `generate.mdc`.
- This file (`workflow.mdc`) governs branching, PRs, CI/CD, and environments.

### CI/CD
- Lint on push; build on PR.
- Deploy `main` to Vercel (frontend). Backend deploy per service (e.g., Render).

### Releases
- Tag notable releases; maintain changelog (optional).

### Testing
- Manual smoke test core flows: nav, add‑to‑cart, signup/login, order.
- Admin: login, view orders, change status, CRUD products.

### Deployment
- Frontend: Vercel with SPA rewrite; set `VITE_API_URL` env.
- Backend: Node/Express app with MongoDB; set required env vars.

